issues.problem:
One item combines unrelated demands that cannot be graded as a unit:
- a conditional ESR response;
- a formatting prohibition (no attachment, no extra pages), which cannot be 'found addressed' in a proposal;
- a budget statement;
- a resource-allocation explanation;
- coverage of four named risk types.
A proposal without an earlier ESR leaves half the item undefined.

Real Cluster 6 topics tie their scope to EU policy and to the destination's expected impacts. This one cites none, so the Impact criterion's reference to 'impacts specified in the work programme' has nothing to link to. Natural anchors exist:
- the integrated urban wastewater management plans for storm water overflows and urban runoff in the recast Urban Wastewater Treatment Directive (EU) 2024/3019;
- short-term pollution management under the Bathing Water Directive 2006/7/EC;
- the Zero Pollution Action Plan.

Horizon Europe topics state an indicative contribution ('around EUR X million') and rarely cap duration. The 36-month cap is also tight for the required work:
- event-based monitoring at contrasting sites;
- calibration data kept separate from independent validation data (SC3);
- co-developed thresholds;
- operational validation (SC6).
Set-up would leave about two storm seasons.
